---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy — nitpick" description="What Nitpick collects and how to turn analytics off.">
  <section class="band"><div class="frame privacy">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>We use PostHog US Cloud to understand how people use Nitpick and to diagnose failures.</p>
    <h2>On this website</h2>
    <p>We collect page visits and times, referrer domains, browser/device information, approximate location, performance metrics, install-prompt copies, demo plays, and outbound-link categories. A random browser ID helps distinguish returning visitors; it does not tell us your name or email.</p>
    <p>We sample 20% of sessions for replay with text and inputs masked and terminal demos blocked. Visits with query strings, fragments, or unknown paths are not recorded. Console output and network request/response bodies are not recorded. Error messages are omitted; diagnostic bundle locations are retained. Analytics URLs omit query strings and fragments.</p>
    <p>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control disable collection. You can also change your preference for this browser:</p>
    <p><button id="analytics-off">Disable analytics</button> <button id="analytics-on">Enable analytics</button></p>
    <p id="analytics-status" role="status"></p>
    <h2>In the CLI</h2>
    <p>Official telemetry-enabled releases send an anonymous installation ID, version, OS/architecture, command category, duration, exit code, aggregate review statistics, public model labels, token counts, provider-reported cost when available, timing, retries, and sanitized failures. These feed product analytics, AI observability, logs, and traces. Custom model names are labeled “other”.</p>
    <p>We do not send source code, diffs, prompts, model responses, findings text, repository names, file paths, API keys, usernames, or raw terminal output to PostHog. CLI IP geolocation is disabled. Website and CLI identities are separate.</p>
    <p>Set <code>NITPICK_TELEMETRY=0</code> or <code>DO_NOT_TRACK=1</code> to disable CLI telemetry before any identity file or network request is made. Hook callbacks, help/version, and <code>nitpick context</code> never send telemetry. Source builds without a project token compiled in do not send telemetry.</p>
    <p>Review code still goes to the model provider you configure; that is separate from analytics.</p>
    <p>Questions or deletion requests: <a href="mailto:rasul@lvtd.dev">rasul@lvtd.dev</a>. CLI installation IDs are stored at <code>~/.local/state/nitpick/telemetry/installation-id</code> (or under <code>XDG_STATE_HOME</code>).</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
<script>
  import { optIn, optOut } from "../lib/analytics";
  const status = document.querySelector("#analytics-status");
  document.querySelector("#analytics-off")?.addEventListener("click", () => { optOut(); if (status) status.textContent = "Analytics disabled for this browser."; });
  document.querySelector("#analytics-on")?.addEventListener("click", () => { optIn(); if (status) status.textContent = "Analytics enabled unless your browser sends a privacy signal."; });
</script>
<style>.privacy { padding: 60px var(--gutter); max-width: 850px; } h2 { margin-top: 32px; } p { margin-top: 16px; line-height: 1.6; } button { padding: 8px 12px; cursor: pointer; } button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ink); outline-offset: 2px; } code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }</style>
